WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:04.880
The Despicable Me movies are always stuffed
with stacks of pop culture references and

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.689
easter eggs that can be lots of fun for fans
to uncover.

00:00:07.689 --> 00:00:11.990
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and I've scoured Despicable Me 3 for easter

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.740
eggs, funny references, plus other cool things
you might have missed, and I'm going to be

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.890
revealing all of them in this video.

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:21.160
I've got a bunch of cool merchandise from
the movie to give away.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.680
So, make sure you subscribe and turn on your
notifications, and answer the question I'll

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.369
be asking later in the video!

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:31.460
A quick reminder also, that there are some
spoilers in this video, so take care if you

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.310
haven't seen the movie yet.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:37.790
Let's kick off with a very cool easter egg
to Illumination's next animated movie "How

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.800
The Grinch Stole Christmas" which stars Benedict
Cumberbatch in the title role.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.240
You can spot the grouchy Grinch character
from the movie and the book of the same name

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.690
by Dr. Seuss on Margot's T-shirt in Despicable
Me 3.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:52.650
But this isn't the first time that Illumination
has featured one of their upcoming films in

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.650
this way.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:58.100
If you look back at the first Despicable Me
movie which was released in 2010, you'll see

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.220
that Margot wore a T-shirt with a picture
of The Lorax on it, and that character popped

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.940
up in his own movie two years later.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:10.380
Agnes's unicorn obsession continues in Despicable
Me 3 and there's a funny call-back to the

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.840
unicorn toy from the funfair in the first
movie that Gru eventually won for her.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.759
In Despicable Me 3, Agnes wanders into the
Tipsy Unicorn bar in Freedonia where she meets

00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:22.100
a bartender who apparently has a real unicorn
horn.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:26.179
And after she grills him about the unicorn,
she demands to know if it was fluffy and he

00:01:26.179 --> 00:01:31.020
replies with the same words Agnes said in
the first movie "it was so fluffy, I thought

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.500
I was going to die".

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.770
"Look at that fluffy unicorn!"

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:39.700
"He's so fluffy I'm gonna die!"

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:45.110
"You saw a for-real-life unicorn?!

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:49.271
What did it look like?"

00:01:49.271 --> 00:01:50.271
[GASPS]
"Did you pet it?

00:01:50.271 --> 00:01:51.271
Did it smell like candy?!"

00:01:51.271 --> 00:01:52.271
"Was it fluffyrrrrrrrrr?!"

00:01:52.271 --> 00:01:53.950
"It was so fluffy, I thought I was gonna die."

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.819
Villain Con, the supervillain convention for
would-be masterminds and criminals that first

00:01:57.819 --> 00:02:02.450
appeared in the Minions movie, gets a shout-out
in Despicable Me 3 via a poster on the wall

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.670
during this shot with two minions.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:10.209
Gru's resident mad scientist Dr Nefario has
appeared in all the Despicable Me movies so

00:02:10.209 --> 00:02:14.430
far, including a small cameo in the Minions
movie where a young Nefario showcased his

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:17.439
Freeze Ray to a young Gru and his mother at
Villain Con.

00:02:17.439 --> 00:02:21.560
In the third Despicable Me movie though, we
discover that Dr Nefario has accidentally

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.970
frozen himself in carbonite, which is an obvious
hat-tip to Han Solo in Star Wars: The Empire

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:29.000
Strikes Back.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.531
Despicable Me 3 introduces a brand new minion
called Mel, who becomes the leader of the

00:02:33.531 --> 00:02:35.760
banana-loving mischief-makers.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.020
Given that Mel is the new top minion in town,
it seems totally fitting that he was named

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:44.810
after Chris Meledandri, the big boss and founder
of Illumination.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:49.720
And notice how when the minions go to prison,
Mel also literally gets number one billing

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:55.049
with 001 on his prison uniform to indicate
he's the head minion.

00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:59.930
And Mel is not only named after Illumination
boss Meledandri, but Mel's hairstyle is also

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.540
modelled after Meledandri's own hairline!

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.730
In fact, Mel's whole design is based on a
birthday card drawing that Despicable Me 3

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.890
co-director Eric Guillon did years ago of
Meledandri as a minion.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:15.180
Mel is, of course, responsible for the minion
rebellion against Gru, but before that, he

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.849
played a hilarious montage of photos the minions
put together to try and convince Gru that

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:23.000
being bad is so much more fun than being good.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.140
And in one of those shots we can see Gru stealing
a rare artefact that looks a lot like the

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:32.590
Golden Idol that Indiana Jones stole at the
beginning of Raiders of the Lost Ark.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:37.040
After almost all the minions leave, Gru and
company travel to Freedonia to meet his twin

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.189
brother Dru.

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:42.430
Although Freedonia is a fictitious place,
it's actually a real word that originated

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:47.319
just after the American Revolution and later
became popularised in the Marx Brothers comic

00:03:47.319 --> 00:03:51.689
movie Duck Soup about a small country called
Freedonia.

00:03:51.689 --> 00:03:55.970
In Despicable Me 3, Freedonia is hilariously
overrun with pigs.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:04:01.030
The police ride on pigs rather than horses,
one of the license plates reads "FR33 PIG"

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:05.269
and the ceiling in the entrance hall to Dru's
lavish mansion is, as Lucy puts it, like "the

00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:07.379
Sistine Chapel with pigs".

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:10.379
Pigs are also incorporated into almost everything
in Freedonia.

00:04:10.379 --> 00:04:15.680
There's a Cheese Invaders arcade game in the
inn, a pig-manned foosball game, Hog Zoda

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:20.720
and Freedo Kola adverts, and does that map
of Freedonia suggest the island is even shaped

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.610
a bit like a pig?

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:27.110
Back at Dru's mansion, Dru introduces Gru
to his lair which is full of statues of past

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:28.580
villains from their family.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.620
And as they walk past a gunslinger, if you
look carefully in the next shot, you can just

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:37.300
make out the name at the base of the statue
which is "Grutch Cassidy", a reference to

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.800
Butch Cassidy, the real-life Wild West train
and bank robber.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:44.210
And if we look at the rest of the villains
in this hall of infamy, could that be a Gru

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.979
version of Hannibal Lecter?

00:04:45.979 --> 00:04:50.990
Over here this clown-looking Gru might be
a nod to the infamous clown Pennywise from

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.690
the Stephen King novel IT and its upcoming
big-screen adaptation.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:59.620
And next to him that looks a bit like Igor,
the classic hunchbacked assistant to Frankenstein

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.020
or Count Dracula?

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:06.370
And if that is Igor, it might also be a little
tie in or reference to Universal's Dark Universe

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:12.150
as Universal are the parent company of Illumination
who developed the Despicable Me franchise.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:17.460
Gru and Dru are, of course, opposites of sorts,
and the Despicable Me 3 filmmakers have described

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.530
Dru as the "yin to Gru's yang".

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:24.580
And on this theme, the animators have cleverly
snuck in a variety of yin and yang symbolism

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:27.320
into several scenes involving Gru and Dru.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:32.690
First of all, the logo on the side of Dru's
Despicamobile is a riff on the classic Yin-Yang

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:33.820
symbol.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:38.319
And notice how the logo shows up again on
Dru's coffee mug over here.

00:05:38.319 --> 00:05:42.970
Gru and Dru's costumes are also black and
white, the same colours that make up the Yin-Yang

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:48.000
symbol, and later when Gru and Dru are up
on the side of Bratt's fortress, they roll

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:53.009
up into a ball that forms the Yin-Yang symbol
thanks to their black and white costumes.

00:05:53.009 --> 00:05:58.229
Later, after the brothers get inside Bratt's
fortress, Dru makes a sly reference to one

00:05:58.229 --> 00:06:00.319
of my favourite comedy shows.

00:06:00.319 --> 00:06:04.220
Steve Carrell, who voices Gru and Dru, is
probably still best known for his portrayal

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.910
of Michael Scott in the sitcom The Office.

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:11.710
In Despicable Me 3, after breaking into Bratt's
lair, Dru says he's feeling queasy and that

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:13.960
he shouldn't have eaten that pot pie.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:18.400
This is a knowing call-back to the season
5 finale of The Office where the whole office

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:23.319
played an elaborate ruse on Michael so they
could go home early when Michael fell asleep

00:06:23.319 --> 00:06:25.960
after eating a family-sized pot pie.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:31.990
Balthazar Bratt is, of course, the new villain
for Despicable Me 3 and thanks to his obsession

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:37.680
with his former fame as a 1980s child star
and his cancelled TV show Evil Bratt, he brings

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.530
a large amount of 80s references to the movie.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:45.259
80s music runs through the whole film and
I particularly liked Bratt's homage to Michael

00:06:45.259 --> 00:06:50.600
Jackson's moonwalking while Jackson's 1987
hit "Bad" was playing.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:55.460
Bratt also makes a clever 80s Hollywood reference
when he unleashes his evil army of Bratt dolls

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.470
who he calls the "Bratt Pack".

00:06:57.470 --> 00:07:02.750
The Brat Pack (spelled with a single 't')
was a term first used in the 1980s to describe

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:07.430
a group of up-and-coming actors who often
worked together including Emilio Estevez,

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:09.390
Molly Ringwald, and Ally Sheedy.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:14.560
At one point, Bratt also says "I love it when
a plan comes together", which is a nice reference

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:19.590
to Hannibal's famous catchphrase from the
80s TV series The A-Team.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:23.560
The giant Dumont Diamond that Bratt steals
at the beginning of the movie is a riff on

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:28.100
the "Pink Panther" diamond from the 1963 movie
which starred Peter Sellers.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:32.750
Peter Seller's physical comedy and his portrayal
of Inspector Clouseau in The Pink Panther

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:37.031
movies has also been a big influence on all
the Despicable Me movies according to the

00:07:37.031 --> 00:07:40.669
franchise's filmmakers, and you can certainly
see they've drawn inspiration from the style

00:07:40.669 --> 00:07:44.650
of the Pink Panther films for this movie's
closing credits.

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:49.360
The fart gun from Despicable Me 1 and 2 makes
a brief appearance during the opening Illumination

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:54.370
title when one of the minions barges in and
uses the gun to blast the others.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:59.030
The Brad &amp; Gary ice cream that appears in
Despicable Me 3 seems like a funny pun on

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:03.680
the famous ice cream brand Ben &amp; Jerry's,
but it's also an easter egg to Illumination's

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:08.370
short film "Brad &amp; Gary" which was directed
by Despicable Me 3 director Pierre Coffin

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:12.870
who also voiced the character of Brad in that
short film, and is, of course, the voice of

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:15.310
the minions as well.

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:19.031
Illumination's previous movie Sing gets a
fairly obvious shout-out when the Minions

00:08:19.031 --> 00:08:23.190
run into a recording studio where a musical
talent show called "Sing" is being filmed,

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:28.960
and, on the way in to the show, they also
run past some Sing billboards outside.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.690
Inside the studio, the Minions put on a pretty
spectacular performance with their own interpretation

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:37.690
in Minionese of the "Modern Major-General's
Song" from the Gilbert and Sullivan comic

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:40.190
opera The Pirates of Penzance.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:44.350
The Minion dance routine during the song also
made me think back to the wonderful sausage

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:49.320
factory scene in Illumination's The Secret
Life of Pets, both of which were partly inspired

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.700
by the renowned musical choreography of Busby
Berkeley.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:58.000
Later, during the scenes where Bratt's giant
robot is terrorising Hollywood, you can see

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.640
billboards advertising an "Onions" movie.

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.640
Now, given that one of the ads for that film
says 'Coming Soon' and the fact that its title

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:09.180
sounds rather like a play on the word Minions,
I think this is a clever tease to the Minions

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.950
2 movie coming in 2020.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:16.420
Another Hollywood billboard was for "Fast
Car Driver 12", a bit of a joke at the long-running

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:21.330
Fast &amp; Furious franchise which is owned by
Illumination's parent company, Universal!

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:26.920
I also chuckled at the "Giganotosaurus Wrecks"
billboard, clearly a wordplay combination

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:32.120
of the two dinosaurs Giganotosaurus and Tyrannosaurus
Rex, both of which are part of another current

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:35.550
Universal Studios movie franchise, Jurassic
World.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:39.790
The billboard easter eggs are a fun way for
Illumination to reference franchises owned

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:44.170
by their parent company Universal, but I think
they may have also enjoyed poking fun at one

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:48.350
of their major animation rivals, Pixar, during
the underwater scene at the beginning of the

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:52.070
movie when a pair of clownfish suddenly appear
out of nowhere.

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:57.220
Gru, Lucy and the minions blast past the clownfish
on their way to stop Balthazar Bratt from

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:58.600
stealing the Dumont Diamond.

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:03.630
The moment does feel a bit on the nose and
perhaps a little joke at Pixar's Finding Nemo

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:04.870
and Finding Dory.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:10.260
So, which easter egg in Despicable Me 3 did
you like the best and were there any I missed?

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:14.661
And, if there's another sequel, what would
you like to see happen in Despicable Me 4?

